      "width": 640,
      "height": 480,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "OLU",
      "description": "The site of the original Aberystwith and Welsh Coast Railway Pwllheli station The Aberystwith and Welsh Coast Railway (as it was then called) was a forerunner of the Cambrian Railways. This was the site of the original terminus station until extension of the line to the current station nearer the centre of the town, in 1909. After the new station was opened, the area to the right of the line, now an industrial park, remained in use as a goods yard and locomotive servicing point. Old traditions die hard on the railway and the level crossing is still officially known as 'Pwllheli Goods Level Crossing', although the goods station closed many years ago.",
